 "wiki": {
  "title": "Hazel grouse",
  "extract": "The hazel grouse, sometimes called the hazel hen, is one of the smaller members of the grouse tribe of birds. It is a sedentary species, breeding across the Palearctic as far east as Hokkaido, and as far west as central Europe, in dense, damp, mixed coniferous woodland, preferably with some spruce. The bird is sometimes referred to as \"rabchick\" by early 20th century English speaking travellers to Russia.",
